disposition (implementation workflow, post-verdict): transcript above is the reviewer's returned verdict, transcribed verbatim (only this disposition section added). All three findings accepted as binding — each verified against the cited code before repair. Repairs in `crates/sley-vm/src/bootstrap.rs`: (1) `BootstrapProfileInput` carries `types: &TypeEnvironment`; `bootstrap_type_ok` walks named definitions (record fields + variant payloads, unknown definitions fail closed, cycle-safe coinductive accept) and checks `LocalCell` element types; (2) `AdapterInvoke` admission extracted to `admit_bridge_use`, which enforces bootstrap-type membership on the resolved row schemas (relationship-holding float/handle rows are not permitted imports) and falls through to the shared declared-result membership check (no more `continue` bypass); (3) new tests: named-definition inspection (tainted/clean/unknown), cell element types, bridge row + result types. Gate suite 10/0 green (6 prior + 3 finding-driven + 1 coverage rule; an earlier draft of this disposition miscounted as 12 — corrected here, reviewer verdict untouched), clippy `-D warnings` and fmt clean, all 20 closure vectors re-admitted. Delta re-review requested.
